description=Container sorting, supply planning and a versioned supply API for separate mods. Requires B47ANCEDRooms (Workshop item 3820077442) for room designation and delegated room policies. Both area scopes include full carried inventory and configured physical storage. Permissions are enforced at supported server integration checks, not unrelated vanilla actions. Obsolete B47 sorting formats/category rules are removed on authority; native rules, item selections, priorities and owned presets are retained. Back up saves before upgrading. Vanilla categories when used alone. Optional Better Sorting (BetterSortCC), Better Containers (EURY_CONTAINERS / REORDER_CONTAINERS) or Extended Categories (CAExtendedCategories) use native categories. Better Containers and Extended Categories category selections save explicit item choices; reselect after category membership changes. Follow each category mod's compatibility rules. Disable original Quartermaster (Quartermaster) and older B47 sorting copies. Development build: includes Dangerous Load and the physical Building Supply Ledger. Craft paper sheets, inspect storage through server-granted native actions, and copy completed static snapshots to a selected CD at a supported powered desktop. Computers open Windows '93: insert a ledger CD and explicitly run QUARTERMASTER.EXE; CD Writer creates discs. Current safehouse and Rooms privacy is enforced for historical reads. Sorting and Shopping collection require a completed matching paper ledger or a powered computer with a ledger CD in accessible adjacent storage by default. Planning/reading need no supply ledger. Physical Shopping Lists require a notebook and pen/pencil to create/edit, consuming one blank sheet per new named list. Choose carried papers, give them to friends, or hold one in either hand for a checklist HUD. Previous personal plans are preserved for explicit one-time import; server options control physical lists and writing supplies. Server sandbox options control both requirements and nearby-computer range. Ledger protocol 2, movement 10, Shopping 3, Personal 2; native SP and dedicated multiplayer NOT TESTED for this iteration. The shelf experiment remains out of scope.
